    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "plural-body",
        "title": "Mwili: mmoja na wengi",
        "body": [
          "Sehemu nyingi za mwili huongeza **-s**: **eye → eyes**, **hand → hands**, **ear → ears**.",
          "Baadhi ni tofauti: **foot → feet**, **tooth → teeth**. Kumbuka: **hand** ni kiganja, **arm** ni mkono wote; **foot** ni unyayo, **leg** ni mguu wote."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "my-hurts",
        "title": "“My head hurts”",
        "body": [
          "Kiswahili husema **kichwa kinauma**. Kiingereza huongeza mwenyewe: **My head hurts.** **My stomach hurts.**",
          "Kwa homa: **I have a fever.** (Nina homa.) Kuuliza: **What’s wrong?** (Una nini?)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sorry-excuse",
        "title": "“Sorry” na “excuse me”",
        "body": [
          "**Pole** na **samahani** zote mara nyingi ni **sorry** kwa Kiingereza: **Sorry!** unapoomba msamaha, na **I’m sorry** kuonyesha huruma.",
          "**Excuse me** ni kumwita mtu au kupita: **Excuse me, where is the bank?** Kumtakia mgonjwa: **Get well soon!** (Ugua pole!)"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Kwa daktari",
        "body": [
          "Kliniki, daktari ataanza na **What’s the problem?** au **How can I help you?** Jibu kwa sentensi fupi: **My stomach hurts.** **I have a fever.** Mwishoni: **Thank you, doctor.**"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
